<title>NEW ZEALAND: Power NZ delays AGM amid legal wrangling.</title>
<headline>Power NZ delays AGM amid legal wrangling.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Power New Zealand Limited, currently subject to a joint takeover plan by U.S.-controlled Utilicorp NZ and local company Mercury, said on Tuesday it would postpone an annual shareholders meeting until September 11 due to pending legal procedures related to its ownership.</p>
<p>Several legal initiatives have been started by Power NZ's independent directors, relating to a cornerstone agreement between PNZ and Utilicorp, and because of these, and the need to keep shareholders informed of such issues, the company said in a statement it was delaying its planned meeting.</p>
